    <h1>We Saved the Lake by Killing It!</h1>

    <p>Lake Huron is now so clear, scientists can see 80 feet down. Sounds like a success, right?</p>
    <p>Wrong.</p>
    <p>That crystal clarity? It’s the clarity of collapse. Invasive mussels wiped out the plankton. The plankton fed the fish. The fish fed the lake. Now? It's just… silence.</p>
